---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const cards = [
  { id: 'restaurants', num: '01', img: '/images/itinerary/santorini.jpg', alt: 'A table set overlooking the Santorini caldera',
    h: 'Dinner reservations', tag: 'The thing to lock in the same day you book your room', meta: 'Booked · 4–8 weeks ahead in high season',
    desc: 'Santorini&rsquo;s best tables go earlier than almost anywhere else I&rsquo;ve been in Greece. From mid-June through mid-September, the sunset-facing tables at the top restaurants are gone weeks out, and what&rsquo;s left is 6:00pm or 10:30pm. Tell me your dates and I&rsquo;ll book the nights that matter before they&rsquo;re gone &mdash; including the rooms that are effectively closed to walk-ins.',
    notes: [
      ['Omnia at Canaves Epitome.', 'The best meal I had in Greece, and where I&rsquo;d send you for sunset &mdash; Epitome faces an actual sunset into the Aegean rather than a caldera view. It&rsquo;s also one of the harder tables to get at the hour worth having, which is why I go after it first.'],
      ['Lycabettus at Andronis.', 'The famous cliffside room. If you&rsquo;re at Andronis I book this the moment your suite is confirmed; if you&rsquo;re not, it&rsquo;s still worth an evening, and I&rsquo;ll tell you which night to give it.'],
      ['Varoulko at Grace, Imerovigli.', 'Michelin-starred chef Lefteris Lazarou&rsquo;s seafood tasting menu, and he personally visits tables. Distinctly Greek yet modern &mdash; the strongest part of the Grace experience.'],
      ['Selene, Fira.', 'The island&rsquo;s benchmark for a serious modern Greek tasting menu &mdash; Santorini fava, white eggplant, tomatoes, Assyrtiko. Worth the night away from Oia, and worth the driver I&rsquo;ll arrange to get you back.'],
      ['Ammoudi Bay, below Oia.', 'Grilled fish at the water&rsquo;s edge. Go at lunch instead of sunset &mdash; same food, a fraction of the crowd, and you won&rsquo;t be climbing 300 steps in the dark.'],
    ],
    take: 'One good rule: two big dinners across a three-night stay, and let the rest be long lunches. Send me your dates and I&rsquo;ll tell you which of those nights are already tight and what I can still get &mdash; usually within a day.' },
  { id: 'catamaran', num: '02', img: '/images/islands/santorini-divider.jpg', alt: 'A catamaran on the caldera below Oia',
    h: 'Your day on the water', tag: 'The best half-day on the island, chartered properly', meta: 'Best for · honeymoons, anniversaries, anyone skipping the sunset crowds',
    desc: 'Seeing the caldera from the water is the one excursion I&rsquo;d put on essentially every Santorini trip. I book these privately with the crews I use myself &mdash; not through a booking site &mdash; and I place the day where it won&rsquo;t get wrecked by wind or collide with your dinner.',
    notes: [
      ['Saint Yachting.', 'My pick at the top end. Crewed, genuinely five-star service, and they&rsquo;ll do overnight and multi-day charters if you want to fold in another island &mdash; worth asking me about early, because the good boats go first.'],
      ['Oia Sunset Cruise.', 'The one I book for a classic private sunset sail out of Ammoudi &mdash; well run, and the right call if you want the experience without a full yacht budget.'],
      ['Private over shared, always.', 'Shared catamarans run 40&ndash;50 people. A private charter is 4&ndash;5 hours with the hot springs, Red and White Beach, a meal aboard and an open bar &mdash; at your pace. I&rsquo;ll match the boat to your budget rather than the other way around.'],
      ['Consider a morning departure.', 'Calmer water, far fewer boats at the swim stops, and you keep your sunset free for dinner or your own terrace.'],
      ['The Meltemi is real.', 'Summer wind can cancel or reroute a sail with little notice, so I place the charter early in your stay with room to move it &mdash; which you can&rsquo;t do once you&rsquo;ve prepaid a fixed date online.'],
    ],
    take: 'Tell me your dates and who&rsquo;s coming and I&rsquo;ll price the right boat for the right morning &mdash; and hold it before the good crews fill up.' },
  { id: 'beach-clubs', num: '03', img: '/images/hotels/andronis-arcadia-1.jpg', alt: 'Daybeds along the water at golden hour in Santorini',
    h: 'Beach &amp; down days', tag: 'One is plenty &mdash; and it needs a driver and a booking', meta: 'Best for · a break from the caldera, long lunches, younger couples',
    desc: 'Something most first-timers don&rsquo;t realize: there&rsquo;s no swimming from the caldera. The beaches are on the opposite side of the island, 25&ndash;40 minutes from Oia, and they&rsquo;re black or red volcanic sand rather than the white sand people picture. Worth one day, planned &mdash; not worth improvising on a cruise-ship morning.',
    notes: [
      ['Theros Wave Bar, Vlychada.', 'The most design-driven beach club on the island and the one I&rsquo;d book first. Roughly 15 minutes from Fira, open May through October, and beds go quickly in peak season.'],
      ['Perivolos &amp; Perissa.', 'The long black-sand stretch on the southeast coast where most of the island&rsquo;s beach club scene lives. Easy, lively, and a genuine change of pace from Oia.'],
      ['Kamari and Red Beach.', 'Both are worth seeing once. Neither is worth a full day &mdash; Red Beach in particular is more photograph than swim, which is the kind of thing worth knowing before it eats your only beach day.'],
      ['Front-row beds sell out by mid-morning.', 'In July and August a walk-in at the better clubs is a lost afternoon &mdash; so I reserve the beds and the car together, and place the day where it doesn&rsquo;t collide with your dinner.'],
    ],
    take: 'One beach day is plenty on Santorini. If beaches are actually the point of the trip, that&rsquo;s an argument for adding Milos or Paros &mdash; which I&rsquo;ll build in rather than talk you out of.' },
  { id: 'athens', num: '04', img: '/images/islands/athens-hero.jpg', alt: 'Athens at dusk',
    h: 'The Athens add-on', tag: 'Two or three nights, not a layover', meta: 'Best for · bookending the trip, food lovers, first-time Greece',
    desc: 'Most people treat Athens as a gateway to the islands. I think that&rsquo;s a mistake. Give yourself two or three nights and you&rsquo;ll discover one of Europe&rsquo;s most exciting food cities, incredible luxury hotels, and neighborhoods that feel completely different from one another. It&rsquo;s the perfect way to begin or end a trip through Greece.',
    notes: [
      ['Put it at the end, not the beginning.', 'Flying home out of Athens gives you a buffer against a cancelled ferry or a delayed island flight &mdash; and you arrive in the city already unwound.'],
      ['Two nights is the minimum that works.', 'One night is an airport hotel with extra steps. Three is genuinely great.'],
      ['Book the Acropolis early.', 'Timed entry, and the first slot of the morning is the only one worth having in summer.'],
    ],
    take: 'Read the full <a href="/athens.html">Athens guide</a> for where I&rsquo;d stay and how I&rsquo;d spend the days.' },
];
---
<Layout
  canonical="already-booked-santorini.html"
  title="Already Booked Santorini? Start Here | Suites With Keith"
  description="Send me what you've booked and I'll build the rest of the trip around it — the reservations, the boat day, the drivers, the ferries."
  preload="/images/islands/santorini-hero.jpg"
>

<!-- hero -->
<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(76svh,700px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/islands/santorini-hero.jpg" alt="The caldera at Santorini" width="1800" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Santorini &middot; already booked</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top:18px;">Already booked<br><em>your hotel?</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">Send me what you&rsquo;ve booked and I&rsquo;ll build the rest of the trip around it &mdash; the reservations, the boat day, the drivers, the ferries.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="send_reservations" data-gtag-location="hero">Send me your reservations</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- intro -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container ab-intro">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="deck" style="max-width:46ch;">The hotel is the easy part. What makes or breaks a Santorini trip is everything around it.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:58ch;">The dinner you couldn&rsquo;t get a table for, the boat day that sold out, the winery afternoon nobody told you to book a driver for, the ferry that was cancelled the morning you were supposed to fly home. That&rsquo;s the part I take on. Send me your hotel confirmation and your dates, and I&rsquo;ll come back with a plan for the days around it &mdash; tables held at the restaurants worth going to, a private boat on the right morning, a driver for the wine afternoon, and transfers that account for what the Aegean does in August. You keep the room you booked. I build the trip around it.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">I spent four weeks across the Cyclades touring nearly every luxury hotel on Santorini and eating, sailing, and driving my way around the island, so none of this comes off a list &mdash; it comes from having done it. Still deciding on the hotel? Start with my <a href="/santorini-hotels-ranked.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Santorini hotel rankings</a> or the <a href="/santorini.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Santorini guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">What I handle</p>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#inquire"><b>Send me your reservations &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#restaurants">Dinner reservations</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#catamaran">Your day on the water</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#beach-clubs">Beach &amp; down days</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#wineries">The wine afternoon</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#athens">Athens add-on</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#extensions">Paros &amp; Milos extensions</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#logistics">Transfers &amp; ferries</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{cards.slice(0, 3).map((c, i) => (
  <section class={`section${i % 2 === 0 ? ' band on-shadow' : ''}`} id={c.id} style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class={`ab-grid${i % 2 ? ' flip' : ''}`}>
        <figure class="reveal ab-media">
          <img src={c.img} alt={c.alt} width="1800" height="1300" loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" />
        </figure>
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="stamp plain" style={`font-weight:700; color:${i % 2 === 0 ? 'var(--brass-lit)' : 'var(--brass)'};`}>No. {c.num}</span>
          <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;" set:html={c.h} />
          <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;" set:html={c.tag} />
          <p class="stamp plain ab-meta" set:html={c.meta} />
          <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;" set:html={c.desc} />
          <div style="margin-top:22px;">
            {c.notes.map(([b, t]) => <p class="ab-note"><b set:html={b} /> <span set:html={t} /></p>)}
          </div>
          <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p set:html={c.take} /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
))}

<!-- easiest way to start -->
<section class="section" style="padding:64px 0;">
  <div class="container ab-callout reveal">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="display:block; margin-bottom:12px;">The easiest way to start</span>
      <h3 class="display-m">Send me what you&rsquo;ve booked</h3>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:52ch;">Your hotel confirmation and your dates are enough. I&rsquo;ll come back with what I&rsquo;d book around them &mdash; and what&rsquo;s already getting tight on your nights.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href="#inquire">Send your reservations</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- wine afternoon -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="wineries" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The wine afternoon</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">An afternoon I&rsquo;ll build and drive you through</h2>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:62ch;">Santorini&rsquo;s vines are grown in volcanic ash and trained into low baskets against the wind. The wine is unlike anything else in Greece, and a half-day is all it takes &mdash; booked in the right order, with someone else at the wheel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-wine">
      <figure class="reveal" style="margin:0;">
        <img src="/images/islands/santorini-days.jpg" alt="An olive tree above the caldera in Santorini" width="1350" height="1800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%; aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover;" />
      </figure>
      <div class="ledger reveal" style="border-top:1px solid var(--band-hairline);">
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">01</span><span class="d"><b>Vassaltis.</b> Start in the north of the island at the winery I send almost everyone to first. Modern, unfussy, and focused on the wine rather than the view &mdash; which is exactly the right way to begin before your palate is three tastings deep. <span class="ab-wmeta">Pour: Assyrtiko, Nasitis &middot; around 1:00pm</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">02</span><span class="d"><b>Domaine Sigalas.</b> The serious stop. Paris Sigalas built the estate that made the world take Santorini Assyrtiko seriously, and the seated tastings run deep &mdash; old-vine bottlings, aged Nykteri, barrel Vinsanto &mdash; paired with small plates. Add lunch here and let the afternoon stretch. <span class="ab-wmeta">Pour: Kavalieros, Vinsanto &middot; around 3:00pm</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">03</span><span class="d"><b>Venetsanos.</b> Finish on the cliff above Athinios port, cut straight into the rock, with the caldera opening up in front of you. It&rsquo;s the view stop &mdash; and a far calmer one than Santo Wines, which fills with cruise groups at exactly the hour you&rsquo;d want to be there. <span class="ab-wmeta">Pour: Assyrtiko, Nykteri &middot; golden hour</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:40px; max-width:640px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
      <p>Don&rsquo;t drive this yourself. The roads between the estates are narrow, the tastings are generous, and the whole point is not to be watching the clock. I book the tastings in the right order and put a driver on the afternoon &mdash; it&rsquo;s one line on your itinerary and nothing for you to arrange.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- athens add-on -->
<section class="section" id="athens" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ab-grid">
      <figure class="reveal ab-media">
        <img src={cards[3].img} alt={cards[3].alt} width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">No. 04</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;" set:html={cards[3].h} />
        <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;" set:html={cards[3].tag} />
        <p class="stamp plain ab-meta" set:html={cards[3].meta} />
        <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;" set:html={cards[3].desc} />
        <div style="margin-top:22px;">
          {cards[3].notes.map(([b, t]) => <p class="ab-note"><b set:html={b} /> <span set:html={t} /></p>)}
        </div>
        <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p class="ab-take" set:html={cards[3].take} /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- extensions -->
<section class="section" id="extensions" style="padding-top:0; scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Paros &amp; Milos extensions</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Add one island, not three</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cards reveal" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); max-width:760px;">
      <a class="card" href="/paros.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Paros</h3><p>The island I recommend more every year &mdash; beaches, restaurants, and villages that never feel overly polished.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/milos.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/milos-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Milos</h3><p>Volcanic cliffs, white rock formations, and hidden coves &mdash; the island to add if you want to actually swim.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:36px; max-width:640px;">
      <p>Santorini is three to four nights for most people. If you have more time, add a single island and actually settle into it &mdash; three islands in seven nights is really three travel days. Both of these are a straightforward ferry, and I can arrange a private boat transfer if the schedules don&rsquo;t cooperate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- logistics -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="logistics" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container ab-log">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-head" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Getting there &amp; around</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.2rem);">Airport &amp; ferry logistics</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="kv">
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Arriving</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Fly Athens &rarr; JTR &middot; high-speed ferry &middot; private helicopter &middot; private boat transfer</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Getting around</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Private transfers &middot; private driver days &middot; ATV / rental car</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">What I arrange</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Private transfers between airport, port and hotel &mdash; especially in Oia, where the drop-off and your room can be a few hundred stairs apart &mdash; plus helicopters through my <a href="/hoper.html" style="color:var(--brass-lit);">Hoper partnership</a> and private boats for island combinations.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div style="margin-top:20px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/santorini-transfer-cheat-sheet.html">The Santorini transfer cheat sheet &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/greek-ferry-rules.html">5 Greek ferry rules every couple should know &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/santorini-excursions.html">The Santorini excursions guide &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass-lit); margin-bottom:16px;">Rules I&rsquo;d give any client</p>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Never book the last ferry of the day.</b> If it cancels, there&rsquo;s nothing behind it.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Don&rsquo;t fly home the same day you sail.</b> Build in a night. The Aegean does not care about your itinerary.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Two islands per week. That&rsquo;s the limit.</b> Three islands in seven nights is three travel days.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Fast ferries cancel in wind.</b> Slow ones don&rsquo;t, as often. Pack motion sickness patches either way.</div>
      <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:30px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
        <p>You&rsquo;ve done the hard part by choosing the hotel. Send me the confirmation and let me handle the rest of it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- the form -->
<section class="section inquire" id="inquire" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal" style="display:block; margin-bottom:16px;">Send me your reservations</span>
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">Your hotel and dates are enough to start</h2>
    <p class="deck reveal" style="margin:18px auto 0; max-width:38ch;">I&rsquo;ll build the rest.</p>
    <form class="inquire-form reveal" action="https://formspree.io/f/mjgnadov" method="POST" style="max-width:520px;">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Already Booked Santorini — reservation details" />
      <input type="hidden" name="page" value="already-booked-santorini" />
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-name">Name</label>
      <input id="ab-name" type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      <label for="ab-email">Email</label>
      <input id="ab-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      <label for="ab-hotel">Hotel you booked</label>
      <input id="ab-hotel" type="text" name="hotel" placeholder="Canaves Oia Suites" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-dates">Travel dates</label>
      <input id="ab-dates" type="text" name="travel_dates" placeholder="June 2027, 4 nights" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-details">What you&rsquo;ve booked, and anything else &mdash; rough is fine</label>
      <input id="ab-details" type="text" name="details" placeholder="Flights booked &middot; honeymoon &middot; want the boat day" autocomplete="off" />
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Send my reservations</button>
      <p class="note">Rather just forward the confirmation emails? Send them to keith.pence@fora.travel and I&rsquo;ll work from those.</p>
      <p class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
    <p class="small reveal" style="margin-top:26px; color:var(--ash);">Haven&rsquo;t locked in the hotel yet? See <a href="/santorini-hotels-ranked.html" style="color:var(--brass);">the Santorini rankings</a> &mdash; booking through me includes a space-available upgrade, daily breakfast, and a &euro;100 hotel credit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .toc-link { font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brass); text-decoration: none; }
  .toc-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .ab-intro { display: grid; gap: 44px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .ab-intro { grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; gap: 80px; } }

  .ab-grid { display: grid; gap: 40px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.15fr; gap: 64px; }
    .ab-grid.flip .ab-media { order: 2; }
  }
  .ab-grid > * { min-width: 0; }
  .ab-media { margin: 0; position: sticky; top: 84px; }
  .ab-media img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover; }
  .ab-meta { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: .64rem; font-weight: 700 !important; }
  .band .ab-meta { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .ab-note { font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 13px; padding-left: 16px; position: relative; color: var(--ash); }
  .band .ab-note { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .ab-note::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .62em; width: 4px; height: 4px; background: var(--brass); }
  .band .ab-note::before { background: var(--brass-lit); }
  .ab-note b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .band .ab-note b { color: var(--band-ink); }
  .band .verdict { border-left-color: var(--brass-lit); }
  .ab-take :global(a) { color: var(--brass); }

  .ab-callout { background: var(--lime); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  .ab-wine { display: grid; gap: 40px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .ab-wine { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 64px; } }
  .ab-wine > * { min-width: 0; }
